pplication/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"368811d5a0793907c5b39a4cc52cb0e89ad4c1d8e3e6db620cd43d01b250d7fe","event_uuid":"8fde9f40-29a7-49ec-a30d-87f037b07371","position":{"commit_sha":"e6dde243e7910e36a9fa148dbde3931b866177a7","position":"1784912045345779839-8fde9f40-29a7-49ec-a30d-87f037b07371"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d2e7ce21894189103c3c307e719cbd8b734ecc5b41a5dcf6d4128ae43f786009","event_uuid":"2dc486cd-0c44-495e-b6a2-7821a9e8330f","position":{"commit_sha":"6e127a2ded024b2cfd3cb8ad930d6a3e5f1e8135","position":"1785007054875026001-2dc486cd-0c44-495e-b6a2-7821a9e8330f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"af2dc5a82a125f0d3401c64f926ca7e63a67e88d27b98c61c2d71f4d8e45a307","event_uuid":"200e33f2-9c42-4b4a-93e6-bdf02c955c0e","position":{"commit_sha":"530f087f0ce69812dac732873865104607e648f1","position":"1785203991139066001-200e33f2-9c42-4b4a-93e6-bdf02c955c0e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1784669377853295001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f410e520-ea88-4260-8810-2f9ab70f4abc","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"jira-reb-1001"},{"link_uuid":"664badb6-8da1-4d8a-b0ca-27ab4f68fae3","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2c14-fa5f-1228-4e02"},{"link_uuid":"f815a50a-2d51-4c3a-9bb8-6ffbf1adf10f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8a4b-e8b6-1bf9-48d8"},{"link_uuid":"87af707a-77ef-4e99-b8e5-2c018c2759fd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6118-8fb2-774f-4c5c"},{"link_uuid":"200e33f2-9c42-4b4a-93e6-bdf02c955c0e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7584-b331-72ca-44a5"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nrebar's reusable review system separates four concerns (critical finder → generous verifier →\ndeterministic decision → non-prescriptive coach), and advertises that a **project** may extend\ncode-review with its own criteria via `.rebar/criteria_routing.json`, exactly as plan-review\nalready allows (registry story 5065; ADRs 0015/0016/0017; contract in `docs/llm-framework.md`).\nTwo gaps block that promise:\n\n1. **The generic seam is broken.** A project's overlay merges, but a net-new LLM-backed project\n   code-review criterion is then silently dropped at five runtime points — it is never fanned into\n   Round A/B, never carries a logical id, never consulted through repository-aware Pass-3 routing,\n   and is rejected by the eval surface and the CLI (root cause proven on superseded bug 8a4b:\n   `criterion_prompt_id` hardcodes the plan-review prefix `ids.py:31,42`; `CodeReviewBatchRunner`\n   iterates only static built-ins `batch_runner.py:49,79`; Pass 3 uses the packaged routing map\n   `workflow_ops.py:419,427`; `_code_review_prompt_id`/`calibrate_criterion` exclude project ids\n   `eval_solver.py:187-201`, `eval.py:416-420`; the CLI admits only plan-review ids\n   `_llm_eval_commands.py:143-155`).\n2. **The extension surface is unproven.** No project criterion actually dogfoods the four-phase\n   boundary contract, so boundary drift (severity/disposition/fix-instructions leaking into the\n   finder, etc.) goes uncaught.\n\nThis epic is the single umbrella for both, superseding **jira-reb-1001** (the prior umbrella),\n**story 2c14** (the generic-seam story), and **bug 8a4b** (the seam defect). It fixes the seam as a\nsequenced, single-concern stack, then authors and dogfoods the first project code-review criterion\non top of the now-working seam.\n\n## Decomposition\n\nEight children. The six **seam** children land as an ordered Gerrit stack, each single-concern on\na **disjoint** production-file set, each growing one RED→GREEN slice of the shared test file\n`tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py` so every stacked change lands green. The\ngate-keyed resolver is first because the others consume it; downstream children reference its\nnew symbol in forward/usage tense with a `[rebar:<id>]` citation over a direct `depends_on` edge.\nThe two **feature** children (adopted from the superseded jira-reb-1001) sit on top of the working\nseam.\n\nSeam stack (dependency order):\n1. **Gate-key the criterion-id resolver** (`criteria/ids.py`) — foundation. — `fc72`\n2. **Round-A fan-in + logical-id attribution** (`code_review/batch_runner.py`,\n   `workflow/gate_dispatch.py`) — depends on 1. — `761e`\n3. **Pass-3 effective routing** (`code_review/workflow_ops.py`) — depends on 2. — `58ef`\n4. **Eval-path admission** (`evals/eval_solver.py`, `evals/eval.py`) — depends on 1. — `8153`\n5. **CLI admission** (`_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py`) — depends on 4. — `41e2`\n6. **Docs contract** (`docs/llm-framework.md`) — depends on 5. — `19dd`\n\nFeature children (on top of the seam):\n7. **Author `project.review-phase-boundaries` + eval corpus** — depends on 5 (eval/CLI surface). —\n   `225a`\n8. **Dogfood the criterion in advisory Gerrit review** — depends on 7. — `9447`\n\nNo two seam children touch the same production file; child 3 is the only consumer of the\nalready-existing `registry.effective_routing` (story 5065), so no child re-implements routing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All eight children exist under this epic in the dependency order above, and each seam child\n      (1–6) passes `rebar review-plan <child>` with no blocking finding; verified by\n      `rebar list --parent 119f-63e3-34b7-4f96` showing eight children and a PASS attestation on\n      each seam child.\n- [ ] Each root-cause seam point is covered by exactly one seam child with no file overlap;\n      verified by cross-checking each seam child's `## Scope` against the five drop points named\n      above (one child per point, disjoint production files).\n- [ ] The epic supersedes jira-reb-1001, 2c14, and 8a4b, and all three are closed; verified by\n      `rebar show 119f-63e3-34b7-4f96` listing three `supersedes` edges and\n      `rebar show <each>` reporting `status=closed`.\n- [ ] The two feature children (225a author, 9447 dogfood) are present and dependency-ordered on\n      the seam; the dogfooding outcome is tracked as [operator-attested] on child 9447 (ADR 0043),\n      not re-verified here; confirmed by `rebar show 9447-b31c-e0b7-446d` depending on 225a.\n- [ ] The overlay-absent runtime keeps the exact ordered 13 built-in batch, unchanged packaged Pass-3 dispositions, and the default plan-review resolver mapping; verified after the seam children land by rtk .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py -k \"resolver or fan_in or parity or routing\", whose parity cases compare the no-overlay batch/dispositions with the packaged built-ins and default resolver outputs.\n- [ ] A project code-review criterion activated in `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` executes **once**\n- [ ] An overlay-absent repo behaves **byte-identically** to today; the 13 built-in overlays are\n- [ ] The `project.review-phase-boundaries` criterion and its balanced eval corpus exist (child 225a)\n- [ ] The runtime contract is documented in `docs/llm-framework.md` (child 19dd).\n- [ ] jira-reb-1001, 2c14, and 8a4b are superseded by this epic and closed.\n","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","761e-5af2-ed57-408a"],["depends_on","8153-e9b5-5706-49c8"],["parent","jira-reb-1001"],["relates_to","6118-8fb2-774f-4c5c"],["relates_to","7584-b331-72ca-44a5"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"","parent_status_uuid":"a0f5aa15-b7cf-4c7b-977b-1d6f686271c3","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["review-architecture","project-criteria","integration"],"ticket_id":"119f-63e3-34b7-4f96","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Thread project code-review criteria through the four-pass code-review seam","verify_commands":[{"command":"rtk .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py -k \"resolver or fan_in or parity or routing\"","dd_id":"DD-EPIC-PARITY","dd_text":"No-overlay runtime preserves the ordered 13 built-ins, packaged Pass-3 dispositions, and default plan-review resolver mapping"}]},"source_event_uuids":["5268e635-3d7e-44dd-8e40-d38bc2ca6fd1","d32cc989-0fbb-4f53-9185-1438e089ef5e","785f72ea-6b53-4d12-b215-41ff282e3f28","d8975d9b-b302-441f-a28c-e05c622e80a0","f410e520-ea88-4260-8810-2f9ab70f4abc","664badb6-8da1-4d8a-b0ca-27ab4f68fae3","f815a50a-2d51-4c3a-9bb8-6ffbf1adf10f","27f5a6e8-ffac-4c7e-8c33-2c8a825ffea1","71eb1680-4f4e-460a-ac3e-ec86dbd14246","d1857a2c-d1c6-4bf9-a2ec-d33f0a8f14a1","95227a9c-3383-4e41-bc09-f80a5f524d7f","d825b8b4-ab97-4a83-842b-8faa91a4085e","87af707a-77ef-4e99-b8e5-2c018c2759fd","df5175aa-972e-4b46-b44d-808f7af46bc5","933535ef-35cc-48e8-bb58-d5ba78850dab","63019e86-a39e-45b9-bdc0-766a32b6b31d","a0f5aa15-b7cf-4c7b-977b-1d6f686271c3","da3a45d2-d07c-4dda-bb62-0e